        <item>
            <title>0.2</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 17:36:24 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>194</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
p { margin: 4px 0 10px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 194)</h2>
<p><b>Shared reviews now work with anyone, anywhere</b> — not just people on your network.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Session ▸ Invite a Reviewer…</b> produces one invite that works for everyone. It tries a direct connection first — instant, and involving nobody else — and falls back to a relay a few seconds later if that machine can't be reached from where they are. Neither of you has to know which one they got.</li>
<li>A client on their own broadband, behind NAT or hotel wifi, can now join a live review with <b>nothing to install and nothing to configure</b>. Both ends connect outward, so there's nothing to open on your router.</li>
<li><b>The relay can't read your review.</b> Every message is encrypted with a key derived from a secret that lives in the invite file and is never sent to the relay. Media never crosses it either — as always, each machine plays its own copy at full resolution.</li>
<li>Invites prefer a <b>Tailscale</b> address when you have one, so anyone on your tailnet gets the fast direct path.</li>
</ul>
<p>Also in this build: a connection that can't reach the host now says so instead of sitting on "Connecting…", and a relay that's unavailable degrades to local-network sharing rather than failing the review.</p>
<p><b>Known gap:</b> a dropped relay connection doesn't reconnect itself yet. If a laptop sleeps or the wifi drops mid-review, rejoin from the invite.</p>
]]></description>
